{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK4miFgAZsnAC9uJFSR4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it with a one-line change at `django/db/models/sql/compiler.py:35`. The `expressions`, `ordering` and `queries` test modules pass (513 tests, OK). I did not write a new test for the exact case from the issue.\n\n**Cause:** the regex used to strip `ASC`/`DESC` from each order-by expression was `(.*)\\s(ASC|DESC)(.*)`. Without `re.DOTALL`, `.` doesn't match newlines. So for a multiline `RawSQL`, the captured \"SQL without ordering\" was only the last line. Two different expressions whose last lines matched (like the two `else null end` cases in the issue) were treated as duplicates, and the second one was dropped.\n\n**Fix:**\n```python\nself.ordering_parts = re.compile(r'^(.*)\\s(ASC|DESC)(.*)', re.MULTILINE | re.DOTALL)\n```\nNow `.` also matches newlines, so the captured part is the whole expression up to the final `ASC`/`DESC`. Duplicates are compared on the full SQL instead of just the last line. This also handles the `\\r` line endings the issue warns about. It's the same fix upstream Django used for this bug."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":231,"cache_read_input_tokens":19542,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":231},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d56a871-4d49-47b1-96b9-6f7c9f79dc33","uuid":"1c2fbfd9-5a1c-4369-a38c-222dcd68cdeb","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:24:33.862Z","request_id":"req_011ChK4mi6VmzbMKDb8dLwsm"}
